the --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification CAUTION is emitted via log() before the markdown fence — ADOPT-001 §12.8 claims it appears 'in the invocation log block' but an operator who pastes only the ~~~markdown block omits the bypass signal from the formal audit trail; (3) no test validates working-tree-only (uncommitted) prior restore evidence detection — all run_enable_case tests commit the log before exercising Gate 3, leaving R8-SAFE-002 closure unverified. Four MIN findings: unknown top-level fields pass through restore transform; enforce_admins.enabled not type-validated as boolean; tag SHA pagination capped at 100 with no loop; branch-name substring ambiguity in prior_restore_evidence_present.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MAJ-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"CI workflow paths + paths-ignore coexistence is invalid per GitHub Actions docs, creating a potential CI enforcement bypass for cohort onboarded PRs.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"check-invocation-log-entry.yml lines 17-24 define both `paths` and `paths-ignore` for the same pull_request event. GitHub Actions docs state these cannot be combined. Under the per-PR interpretation ('no changed file matches paths-ignore'), a 024C PR touching both DISPATCH-NOTE (matches paths:024[C-Z]*/**) and branch-protection-log.md (matches paths-ignore) would not trigger the workflow, silently bypassing CI enforcement. The job-body short-circuit only fires if the workflow is triggered at all.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If GitHub evaluates paths-ignore at PR scope rather than per-file, every cascade-status:onboarded PR (which must modify branch-protection-log.md per invariant 2) would bypass the CI gate. Plan-doc invariant 2's CI-enforcement claim would be unenforceable at the automation layer.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Remove paths-ignore entirely from the workflow. The paths filter already excludes 024[AB]*/** (starts at 024[C-Z]*/**). The job-body short-circuit (lines 46-63) already handles PRs with no cascade DISPATCH-NOTE. Drop branch-protection-log.md and STATUS.md from both paths and paths-ignore; they are not needed as workflow triggers.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MAJ-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Gate 2 bypass CAUTION is not inside the invocation log block; ADOPT-001 §12.8 claim is inaccurate and the audit trail is incomplete.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh line 502 emits the CAUTION via log() before the log block fence. check_forward_mode_safety (line ~484) emits a second log() CAUTION line, also before the ~~~markdown fence. The structured log block (lines 804-874) contains no field recording ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION state. ADOPT-001 §12.8 explicitly states: 'the helper emits a caution line in the invocation log block so the bypass is visible in the audit trail.' The markdown fence is what operators paste into branch-protection-log.md.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An operator following the 'Append the block below' instruction pastes only the ~~~markdown...~~~ section, omitting the pre-block CAUTION lines. Gate 2 bypass is invisible in the formal audit trail. D-047 trust-model claim that the bypass is 'auditable via CAUTION log entry' is inaccurate as currently implemented.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a structured field inside the ~~~markdown log block: `- **Gate-2-bypass:** yes (--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification supplied)` when ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION=1. This ensures the bypass flag is captured in the pasteable audit artefact regardless of whether the operator includes pre-block stdout.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MAJ-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"No test covers the working-tree-only (uncommitted) prior restore evidence path; R8-SAFE-002 closure is unverified by the test suite.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"prior_restore_evidence_present() in enable-required-check.sh reads both cat log_path (committed) and git diff HEAD -- log_path (working tree). But every run_enable_case test in the test file that exercises Gate 3 (lines 2084-2250) calls commit_case before running the enable, placing restore evidence in committed HEAD. There is no test where the log entry is written to the working tree but not committed to HEAD before the Gate 3 forward-mode invocation.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If git diff HEAD returns empty in some environments (e.g., detached HEAD, dirty index assumptions), the working-tree detection silently fails. An operator who runs Gate 1 --restore, logs the entry to branch-protection-log.md but forgets to commit before running Gate 3, would bypass the --expected-wrapper-sha requirement with no error. R8-SAFE-002 carry-forward is marked closed without a passing test.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a test case: write restore evidence to branch-protection-log.md in the working tree (do not commit), then invoke the forward-mode enable and assert exit 2 with 'prior --restore evidence detected' (requiring --expected-wrapper-sha). Also verify that the awk extraction correctly strips leading + from diff output lines.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MIN-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"validate_restore_source_json passes unknown top-level fields through the transform without a closed-set allowlist.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The Python transform (enable-required-check.sh lines 350-366) iterates all keys and skips only {_links, url, checks, required_signatures}. Fields like allow_force_pushes, allow_deletions, lock_branch, required_linear_history pass through unchanged. GitHub branch protection PUT accepts these fields. A crafted before-JSON with allow_force_pushes:true would restore with force-pushes re-enabled. The posture-degradation guards cover only enforce_admins.enabled and contexts length.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Operator who provides a wrong before-JSON file (e.g., from a test fixture or another repo) could inadvertently restore with weakened protection settings (e.g., allow_deletions:true) without any acknowledgement flag requirement. Not exploitable without operator cooperation, but violates principle of least-privilege for the restore primitive.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a top-level closed-set filter to the transform output: only emit keys in {required_status_checks, enforce_admins, required_pull_request_reviews, restrictions}. Log a warning for any additional keys stripped from the input. This matches the forward-mode build_payload structure and prevents accidental field passthrough.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MIN-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"validate_restore_source_json does not type-validate enforce_admins.enabled as a boolean, allowing string 'false' to coerce to Python True, masking the admin-removal posture-degradation guard.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"required_types validates enforce_admins as dict but not its .enabled sub-field. Python bool('false') = True (non-empty string). A before-JSON with {\\\\\\\"enabled\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"false\\\\\\\"} would produce enforce_admins:true in the transform output, causing RESTORE_TARGET_ADMINS_ENABLED='true' and skipping the guard. The GitHub API always returns boolean for .enabled, but the validation does not enforce this.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"In practice, GitHub API never returns string-typed booleans, so this is not exploitable against real API output. However, a manually-crafted or accidentally-corrupted before-JSON could pass the guard when it should require acknowledgement, resulting in admin enforcement being silently removed from the restore target.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a type check: if not isinstance(data['enforce_admins'].get('enabled'), bool): sys.exit(2). Similarly validate required_status_checks.contexts as a list of strings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MIN-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags is capped at 100 tags with no pagination loop; valid release-tag SHAs beyond page 1 produce spurious exit-2 rejections.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh line 431: gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/refs/tags?per_page=100 — single call, no Link-header pagination. A repo with >100 tags would not have tags beyond position 100 checked. A valid --expected-wrapper-sha from a release beyond position 100 would fail 'not found in release-tag SHA cache' and force the operator to use --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification — the escape hatch the check is designed to make optional.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"As the SCP repo accumulates >100 release tags (unlikely in the near term but certain over months of active releases), Gate 3 validation degrades from a real check into a denial that forces the escape hatch. The bypass protection is progressively undermined over time without any visible signal.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a pagination loop over Link headers in the tag list response, or use a targeted tag-SHA resolution via the single-tag API endpoint (gh api repos/.../git/ref/tags/<known-release-tag>) if the operator also supplies the release tag name alongside the SHA.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MIN-004\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"prior_restore_evidence_present uses awk index() substring match, causing false-positive Gate 3 enforcement when branch names are substrings of each other.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh lines 410-424: awk target match is index(line, target) > 0. Target is REPO@BRANCH (e.g., jrnb2024/pim@main). A log section header for jrnb2024/pim@main-old contains jrnb2024/pim@main as a substring, so index() > 0 is true. awk would incorrectly detect prior restore evidence for jrnb2024/pim@main when only a jrnb2024/pim@main-old entry exists.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"False positive: Gate 3 incorrectly requires --expected-wrapper-sha for a first-time enable on a repo whose log has a prior entry for a differently-named branch. Causes unnecessary friction and may push the operator toward the --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification escape hatch. Not a bypass (more restrictive than intended).\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Anchor the section-header match: use index(line, \\\\\\\" \\\\\\\" target) > 0 or a regex match requiring a word boundary after BRANCH (e.g., line ~ (\\\\\\\"^### .* \\\\\\\" target \\\\\\\"$\\\\\\\") using gawk, or append a sentinel character to the target). The log format is ### TS — REPO@BRANCH, so appending a trailing space or end-of-line anchor is sufficient.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"ea775e56-88f5-4773-b99a-f3e161ca5fb3\",\"total_cost_usd\":0.88730075,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":11,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":87267,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":456675,\"output_tokens\":28080,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":87267,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":4232,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":91556,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3092,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":3092},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1669,\"outputTokens\":29,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.0018139999999999999,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":11,\"outputTokens\":28080,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":456675,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":87267,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.88548675,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"9e92c2cb-40dd-4ba1-9fa8-783da3f90f68\"}\n\n---FILE---\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":592876,\"duration_api_ms\":594004,\"num_turns\":22,\"result\":\"Now I have enough information to produce the structured findings report.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CHANGES_REQUESTED\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"024B-extras core deliverables are present and correctly wired: --restore mode logic (GET→PUT transform, APPLY_FAIL wrap, posture-degradation flags, required_signatures sub-resource, working-tree prior-entry detection), forward-mode safety check (path-pinned workflow lookup, no branch filter, release-tag SHA validation), ADOPT-001 §12.8 3-gate break-glass, CI workflow, run_restore_case + make_restore_fake_gh test helpers, D-047, and VERSIONING.md branch-protection helper flag list — all present and spec-compliant. Carry-forward items R8-CORR-001/003 confirmed closed in 024B-core; R8-CORR-002 (restore-mode guard scoping) correctly addressed; R8-SAFE-001 WARNING+CAUTION+D-047 acknowledgement complete; R8-SAFE-002 working-tree diff check present; R8 bootstrap paths-ignore + case-statement tooling-slice short-circuit present. Plan-doc §6 024B split note correctly gates 024C on both halves + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001. TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001 correctly tracked in STATUS.md as merge-blocking open TF; AC checkbox correctly unchecked. Two MAJ findings block fixpoint: the scope-deliverable placeholder file is absent despite STATUS.md claiming it was recorded, and the dual-listing of branch-protection-log.md and STATUS.md in both paths and paths-ignore creates an enforcement bypass risk under GitHub's whole-PR trigger evaluation semantics. Two MIN documentation gaps: FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001 closure not noted in STATUS.md chain, and extras-parking branch deletion guidance absent.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MAJ-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Scope-deliverable placeholder file restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md does not exist in the branch, but STATUS.md 024B-extras chain item 4 states 'placeholder path recorded at docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md', implying the file was created.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Glob for 'docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence*.md' returned empty. DISPATCH-NOTE scope table lists this path as a deliverable with '**MERGE-BLOCKING**' marker and 'The placeholder path is the handoff target until the operator completes the demo.' STATUS.md item 4 contradicts the empty-Glob result.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"The handoff target for the operator-interactive step-7 demo is undocumented as a file artifact. The AC is correctly unchecked and TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001 is tracked, but the stub file required to close the scope-table deliverable is absent, creating a STATUS.md-vs-branch discrepancy.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Create a stub docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md containing the evidence template fields (repo, operator, timestamp, before-state ref, after-state ref, byte-match assertion result) with a PENDING header. This is the Codex scope deliverable; the operator replaces it with real evidence at step 5.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MAJ-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"branch-protection-log.md and STATUS.md appear in BOTH paths and paths-ignore in the CI workflow trigger. Under GitHub's whole-PR evaluation semantics (if ANY file in the PR matches paths-ignore, the workflow does not trigger), an onboarded cohort PR that modifies a cascade DISPATCH-NOTE AND branch-protection-log.md would silently skip enforcement — defeating plan-doc invariant 2's CI-enforced component.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\".github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml lines 19-27: paths lists 'docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md' and 'STATUS.md'; paths-ignore repeats both. GitHub trigger evaluation semantics are debated between per-file (workflow triggers if ANY file matches paths but not paths-ignore) and whole-PR (workflow blocked if ANY file matches paths-ignore). The DISPATCH-NOTE spec intentionally included both; the job-body short-circuit provides a safety net only if the workflow triggers at all.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If GitHub evaluates whole-PR: every cascade-status=onboarded PR (which modifies branch-protection-log.md) would bypass CI enforcement entirely. The required-status-check would be registered but would never run, making it a nominal gate rather than a real one. Invariant 2 'CI-enforced' would be unmet.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Remove branch-protection-log.md and STATUS.md from paths-ignore. The job-body short-circuit (gh pr diff --name-only finds no cascade DISPATCH-NOTE → exit 0) already handles log-only or status-only PRs correctly. Removing these from paths-ignore eliminates the ambiguity with no correctness regression.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MIN-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001 remains listed as open in STATUS.md despite the 024B-extras workflow implementation effectively addressing the concern (tooling slices exit 0 via case statement before script invocation; --allow-not-applicable is omitted from the workflow invocation).\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"STATUS.md 'Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-024 024B-core / 024B-extras' lists FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001 as open. The 024B-extras chain (4 items) contains no closure or update note for this FUP. Workflow lines 55-61: case statement for 024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024G exits 0; workflow line 72-76: check-invocation-log-entry.sh invoked without --allow-not-applicable.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Post-extras merge, the FUP remains open, creating audit trail confusion when 024C opens. If a 024C reviewer reads STATUS.md, the open FUP implies the workflow bypass surface is still unresolved when it is actually addressed.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a note to the 024B-extras STATUS.md chain: 'FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001 addressed — job-body case statement hardcodes tooling-slice exit-0 before script invocation; --allow-not-applicable omitted from cohort-check invocation. Closure approach differs from --tooling-slice-id flag but achieves same bypass-surface elimination.' Mark as closed or pending-confirm.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MIN-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The STATUS.md 024B-extras chain entry contains no note about the extras-parking branch lifecycle (feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking can be deleted once both 024B-core + 024B-extras merge). The review focus explicitly requires this note.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"STATUS.md 024B-extras chain (4 items; lines 153-158) contains no reference to feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking branch deletion. Review focus item 6: 'STATUS.md chain entry. Documents extras outcome + step-7-demo evidence reference + extras-parking branch closure note (the parking branch can be deleted once both halves merge).'\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"The parking branch persists post-merge with no documented lifecycle endpoint. Minor audit trail clutter; a future 024C author may be uncertain whether the parking branch is still active.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Append to the 024B-extras STATUS.md chain: 'Branch feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking may be deleted once both 024B-core (249aa9f) and 024B-extras have merged — R8 carry-forward audit trail is preserved in the parking branch commit history and r8-archive directories.'\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-nit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags queries tags with per_page=100 and no pagination loop; SHAs from tags beyond position 100 would not be found.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"scripts/enable-required-check.sh line 432: gh api 'repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/refs/tags?per_page=100'. No --paginate flag or loop. Current SCP tag count is well under 100; forward-compat only.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"At current scale, no impact. Becomes a silent validation bypass if SCP ever cuts more than 100 release tags.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add --paginate to the gh api call or note the 100-tag limit in a comment. Low urgency given current tag count.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-nit-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"STATUS.md 024B-extras chain item 2 describes the CI workflow paths-ignore as 'docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**' only, omitting branch-protection-log.md and STATUS.md from the summary.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"STATUS.md line 156: 'paths-ignore: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**'. Actual workflow paths-ignore has 3 patterns: 024[AB]*/**/**, branch-protection-log.md, STATUS.md.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Minor audit trail fidelity gap. No correctness impact.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Expand STATUS.md item 2 to list all three paths-ignore patterns for faithful documentation.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"d4e6346a-81db-4baf-aa71-6220e782ef74\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.1286729000000002,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1117,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\