igned`) — 8-criterion checklist for operator sign-off when ≥3 adopters (FLA mandatory) opted in + first weekly aggregator clean. Closed TF-023D-003: `_log_tool_invocation` now reads active key_id from `docs/security/mcp-signing-keys.pub` via new `_resolve_audit_key_id()` helper (graceful fallback `key-ring-unreadable` if key ring empty/malformed; never blocks tool calls). Updated `test_stdio_handshake.py` expected tools list to include `consult_scorecard`. 86/86 MCP tests pass. **fix-round-3:** Two real CI gaps surfaced — (1) SCP-self opt-in attempted then reverted because GitHub blocks `actions/attest-build-provenance` on user-owned private repos (filed TF-023E-001). (2) Wrapper SHA pin bump (v1.0.0 → @5ff2acd) reverted because GitHub Actions validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow at startup (BEFORE `if:` evaluation), and the `attest-scorecard` job's `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` exceed the wrapper's ceiling — startup_failure even with `scorecard-emit: false` (filed TF-023E-002 — restructure policy-check.yml so attest-scorecard is a separate top-level workflow file). USER-GATE-D criterion (i) updated: SCP-self carve-out — satisfied set is now `FLA + ≥2 of {PIM / recommender / mapp-doc-agent / control-tower}`. R1/R2 adversarial review missed both constraints (only visible at actual CI runtime in this repo's specific visibility/ownership context). Wrapper stays pinned at v1.0.0 (@41a5299) until TF-023E-002 closes. Merged at `295e0da`. |\n| 6 | #102 | **024A** | WP-SCP-024 plan-doc v0.1 — estate cascade. Defines adopter cohort `{pim, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower}` (per D-035) explicitly **FLA-independent** per operator direction; canary-first sequencing PIM → control-tower → mapp-doc-agent + recommender → shopify-app; per-adopter onboarding contract (adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice + invocation log + post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle). Reserves D-044/D-045/D-046 for implementation slices 024B/024C/024G. Threshold A: ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters required-check live + ≥1 SCP minor version-bump propagated cleanly via Renovate + USER-GATE-E signed. Required-check cascade is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure, and 024B-core now warns on post-v1.2.0 SHAs while keeping the v1.0.0 pin as the operational fallback until TF-023E-002 closes. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\n\n## Today's chain (2026-05-09 — D-035-rules retired + WP-SCP-025 parked)\n\n**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** the 6 D-035-aligned rules previously framed as gating CT Wave 1 entry on 2026-05-15 are **RETIRED under that deadline** — re-scoped under WP-SCP-025 (parked, post-WP-SCP-024 Threshold A). The retirement is conditional on a strategic reframe: SCP's near-term credibility depends on shipping 2-3 high-value domain rules that catch things review misses + measurable adopter consumption (≥3 cohort adopters running ≥2 SCP-R-005+ rules with ≥80% pass rate over ≥4-week observation window), not on forcing the 6 SDK-discipline rules through under deadline pressure when (a) CT D-035 Phase 5 already shipped 2026-05-07 without these rules as preconditions; (b) WP-SCP-024 cascade is operator-decided FLA-independent per 2026-05-03 §2 invariants row 4; (c) none of the 6 had been drafted with 6 days remaining; (d) parallel work on slice 024B (the actual cascade gate per plan-doc §6) would have been diluted.\n\n**The 6 retired rule names** (preserved here for traceability — re-evaluate at WP-SCP-025 kickoff against the §4 candidate list in the parked plan-doc):\n1. `sdk_version_pin` (was Wave 1 gate)\n2. `ct_sdk_conformance` (was Wave 1 gate)\n3. `sdk_migration_waiver` (was Wave 1 gate)\n4. `sdk_adoption_schedule` (was Wave 1 mid)\n5. `bff_refresh_hardening` (was Wave 2 gate)\n6. `ct_auth_provider_memoization` (was Wave 3 gate)\n\n**Cross-project reconciliation:** SCP filed `SCP-D035-RULES-RETIRED-2026-05-09.md` to CT governance notifications log requesting CT amendments to (a) `docs/briefings/recommender-shopify-j1-rbac-response-2026-05-09.md` Q6+Q8 to drop the 6-rules / 2026-05-15-deadline framing before the response ships, (b) `docs/plans/PLAN-CT-D-rollout.md` §3 WP-D-SCP entry to point at WP-SCP-025 backlog. CT-owned changes; SCP requesting explicitly so cross-project view stays consistent.\n\n**Forward work:** WP-SCP-025 (`docs/plans/WP-SCP-025-domain-rules-v1.md`) parked with 5 candidate rules (protected_tables_updated_with_migration / r1_evidence_linked_in_pr_body / waiver_expiry_within_window / secrets_not_in_committed_env_files / permission_schema_registered_within_wave_window) for WP-SCP-025 owner to review and pick 2-3 from at scoping time. Owner: TBD (named at parked-plan kickoff post-024 Threshold A).\n\n**Slice 024B-core remains the immediate work** — hard predecessor for cohort onboarding 024C-F per WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §6. Scope: scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + tests; 024B-extras deferred.\n\n## Today's chain (2026-05-09 PM — slice 024B-core + scope-split decision)\n\n**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** WP-SCP-024 slice 024B split into 024B-core (scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + cascade-status CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (`--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Empirical justification: original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code; R6 missed a primary deliverable; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR. Surface-area-too-large for single-pass convergence. Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope — both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens.\n\nOriginal 024B work preserved at branch `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` (pushed to origin 2026-05-09; audit trail intact: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log + 7 R-round archive dirs).\n\n| # | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Slice 024B-core: `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` + `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` + `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` (CLI) + `tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh` + `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` (cascade-status enforcement only). D-044 filed scoped to core. Branch: `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-core`. |\n| 2 | Slice 024B-extras: deferred. Scope: `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` + step 7 operator-interactive `--restore` round-trip demo. To be branched from merged 024B-core. R8-CORR-001/002/003 (extras-parking r8-archive) carry forward as known findings. |\n| 3 | Plan-doc §6 amendment: 024C entry now conditional on BOTH 024B-core + 024B-extras merged + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure (was: 024B + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure). Cohort cascade gate unchanged in posture; precondition list extended for clarity. |\n\n## Today's chain (2026-05-10 — slice 024B-extras)\n\n| # | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Slice 024B-extras: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore` added with GET-shape → PUT-shape transform, posture-degradation acknowledgements, required-signatures sub-resource handling, and forward-mode safety checks (path-pinned workflow lookup, no branch filter on runs API, release-tag SHA validation,